@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] build-v2-opt-in
The crate MUST remain independent of production v1 until a separately validated caller cutover.
A0 schemas MUST NOT decide cache hits, launch native tools or publish results.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-summary-observation
Explanations MUST consume existing typed decisions and compact original-ingredient metadata without
extra source/payload/cache reads, execution capabilities or provenance/platform key additions.
Submission MUST NOT imply a launch, and incomplete lifecycle reports MUST NOT prove zero launches.
Identity-only resolution and uninstalled hits MUST NOT count as restored. Successful publication
before later settlement failure MUST remain visible; errors MUST preserve publication/effect
uncertainty rather than certify no writes. Missing records/objects MUST NOT imply eviction.
See tests/explain.rs, explain_cases in tests/scheduler.rs and python_executor::tests. Changed real
Python/APFS summary assertions in python_backend::tests remain MAC1 pending.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-identity-boundary
Identity ingredients MUST distinguish producing input keys from each output's content digest.
Provenance MUST remain outside identity ingredients. Installed Python, dependencies, lockfiles,
Blender/add-ons, Unreal and compiler/SDK versions MUST NOT automatically become key ingredients;
platform invalidation uses explicit cache/op versions. See tests/interfaces.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-wire-boundary
Worker messages MUST use a separate pipe with a versioned, bounded JSON frame. Unknown message
shapes, unsupported protocol versions and truncated frames MUST fail, as MUST duplicate keys and
positional (array) forms of the envelope, message or any typed record; arrays inside params and
lists remain data. Only EOF between frames may be a clean close. Bulk asset bytes MUST travel in
staged files, not wire messages. See tests/protocol.rs and the shared vectors
tests/vectors/protocol_v1.json checked by tests/worker_session.rs and
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_protocol.py.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-t0-registry
CI MUST compile the current crate successfully before running host tier tests. Its matrix MUST cover
all declared supported host platforms. Every active scenario MUST declare one tier: t0 and t1a run
as the two required steps of that job within ten and thirty seconds respectively, excluding
compilation; t1b (Blender) and t2 (Unreal) are native exclusions and MUST NOT run there. Every
applicable test MUST be assigned to exactly one host tier and have complete, unskipped execution
evidence on each applicable platform; the filters derived from that assignment MUST select exactly
each tier's own tests, including tests that share one binary with another tier. Other-platform
exclusions, native tiers and pending future scenarios MUST be reported separately and MUST NOT count
as coverage.
See tools/check_registry.py and platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_registry.py.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-object-digest-format
Object format version 1 MUST name payload bytes with exactly 64 lowercase SHA-256 hex characters
under objects/sha256. A change to algorithm or encoding MUST use a new object format/namespace.
Filesystem permissions MUST remain result metadata rather than payload identity.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-object-publication
The object store MUST freeze and verify an independent clone before atomic no-replace publication.
Caller-provided unchecked digests MUST NOT certify bytes. Hits MUST clone without rehashing or
scanning output folders; clone failures MUST be explicit and MUST NOT fall back to byte copies.
Existing entries and unrelated checkout/staging files MUST never be overwritten or removed.
See tests/objects.rs; macOS APFS tests are required acceptance evidence.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-worker-session-order
A controller session MUST accept work only after a hello with the expected worker version, MUST
keep at most one active job, and MUST require `started` then exactly one terminal response with
the active job ID. Wrong IDs, duplicate or out-of-order responses, malformed frames and early end
of stream MUST break the session. Sending `cancel` MUST NOT count as cancellation; only a worker's
`cancelled` failure confirms it. A worker MUST send `started` for every `run` before its single
terminal response, including a job it rejects at once and a `cancel` that arrives before it started.
Job requests MUST pass through unchanged. See tests/worker_session.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-result-leases
Result writes MUST have a durable staging lease before payload creation and durable object claims
under the shared metadata mutex before object publication. The order MUST be objects, immutable
result record, required durable build-root callback, then per-unit claim release. Failure before
durable rooting MUST retain claims; no failure may erase earlier results. Live or unknown owners/workers MUST prevent reclamation;
timestamps alone MUST NOT expire leases. See tests/results.rs; B4/B5 implement root/GC policy later.
Initial leases MUST retain supplied upstream result keys while the consumer record is incomplete.
Fresh lease/staging names MUST preserve every occupied entry, including dangling symlinks.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-frozen-result-validation
Output validators MUST read the same frozen snapshots hashed and published by B1. Result winner
comparison MUST include complete fixed and group manifests/projections and semantic modes, but
exclude provenance, unit scheduling labels and upstream retention links. Group publication MUST
require complete actual membership, fixed keyed contracts and sealed frozen-source validation.
External outputs MUST refuse until their typed adapter exists. Cached group tokens MUST issue
only after named object checks and durable pins under the GC mutex, without plan reads, output
tree walks or rehashing. See tests/results.rs and
groups::tests::leased_group_publication_restores_tokens_and_compares_whole_manifest.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] lock-busy-is-transient-under-concurrent-spawn
An ambient CLOEXEC fork copy of a checkout lock descriptor keeps that lock held until the child
execs, so a just-released lock can report Busy. Busy alone MUST NOT be treated as proof that another
owner holds the checkout. A caller that retries MUST bound its own retry and deadline; the library
does not impose one. Explicit custody lasts until its last handle closes, independently of any fork
copy. See tests/checkout_locks_spawn.rs::lock_busy_is_transient_during_spawn.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;safety] build-v2-checkout-install
Checkout installs MUST hold build and exclusive content custody, retain certified source custody
(named cache-object pins for cached restores or durable sealed snapshots for local completions),
and durably journal exact old/new ownership before payload staging or mutation. They MUST use
clone-only restoration and recorded normalized modes, without payload hashing or tree discovery.
Receipt identity MUST include explicit stable project namespace plus logical item path, never
selected roots or Unit.id. Foreign files, other projects and current code/sources MUST be preserved.
Before receipt-index commit recovery MUST restore prior owned bytes; after commit it MUST finish
only exact owned cleanup. Unknown/replaced checkout files or malformed journals MUST retain evidence and
block readers. Required root failure MUST preserve valid installed work and cache claims.
See tests/installs.rs and checkout_locks::tests; macOS APFS acceptance remains mandatory.
An unready journal MAY abort only with the unchanged prior index, exact old file observations,
absent trash and matching pre-owned directory identity. Recovery MUST persist abort intent,
archive the exact SHA-bound journal, durably quarantine the whole scope without replacing
another name, and recheck identities/evidence/old checkout before clearing reader exclusion.
Unknown private leaves MUST be preserved, never adopted/deleted or certified as result bytes.
Quarantine retains independent artifacts and explicit owner/claim metadata; failed B2 leases
remain unchanged. Future dead-producer CAS retention and explicit quarantine cleanup are separate.
Replacement inodes at prior receipt-owned names MUST refuse restore/retirement; dirty original
inodes MAY be journaled using their fresh metadata. ReceiptReader MUST use the shared exact
receipt/stat validator without opening or creating any cache paths, including on cold start.
See preinstall_abort_preserves_unknown_clone_and_resumes_every_durable_cut,
preinstall_abort_rejects_changed_outputs_trash_and_replaced_directory_identities,
replaced_receipt_inode_is_foreign_before_restore_and_whole_item_retirement and
install_modes_receipts_and_clone_independence_survive_cache_removal in tests/installs.rs.

Current receipt validation and install preflight MUST share exact complete owner/index membership;
extra indexed paths MUST NOT certify Current. Cleanup MUST resume safely when an already-removed
owned ancestor is absent, while retaining identity checks for every existing cleanup directory.
Fresh transaction names MUST preserve all occupied transaction/quarantine entries, including
dangling links, so process-ID reuse cannot strand an otherwise valid pre-install abort.
See extra_owner_index_membership_refuses_current_and_restore_without_mutation,
interrupted_cleanup_resumes_after_each_leaf_directory_and_barrier_removal in tests/installs.rs,
and install::tests::scope_allocator_preserves_occupied_transaction_and_quarantine_names.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-python-job-isolation
Each Python job MUST run in its own child of the job loop, in its staged folder, with the declared
environment only, loading only installed platform modules and the unit's declared code; the checkout
MUST NOT be on its import path. The child keeps `-P -s -S` and runs no `.pth` file: installed
libraries come only from the loop's own purelib and platlib folders, passed in the child's private
configuration and appended after the standard library. The installed OpenSSL configuration MAY be
read through the exact canonical literal /private/etc/ssl/openssl.cnf as platform context, not a
new keyed game input; this MUST NOT grant neighboring files, an etc/ssl directory, Mach lookups,
network access or an OPENSSL_CONF override. See the portable profile inspection in
test_build_v2_python_worker.py; actual sandbox execution remains separate guarded evidence.
The child MUST fail the job as
`dependency` before running it when any such folder is missing, relative, not a folder, or resolves
(symbolic links included) outside the approved platform roots. Installed libraries stay platform
context and never enter a key. On macOS the child MUST run under a deny-default sandbox that lets
it execute only the interpreter, and any undeclared read, Python-level existence check (of a present
or missing path), listing, network use or process start MUST fail the job as `dependency` rather
than return a value; writes outside `output/` MUST fail. The production loop entry MUST have no
unsandboxed mode; the only unsandboxed loop is a test-only entry that MUST announce a distinct worker
version, so a session keyed to the production version refuses it. Path checks MUST resolve
descriptor-relative (`dir_fd`) and descriptor-named access against the descriptor's real directory,
and directory changes MUST be refused so relative paths always resolve against the job folder.
Every Python wall-clock read (`time.time`/`time_ns`, default `localtime`/`gmtime`/`ctime`/`strftime`,
`datetime` now/today, `clock_gettime` of realtime clocks) MUST return the fixed instant; `random`
(module functions, `Random()` and argument-less reseeding) MUST use the declared seed; Python OS
entropy APIs MUST raise. The job configuration MUST travel off argv, and a failure to start the job
process MUST still yield its one terminal response. The loop MUST make both protocol descriptors
non-inheritable before any job runs, and MUST report every regular file left under `output/` (fixed
outputs and group members alike), failing on links and special files; the controller decides
membership. Limitations, not guarantees: native extension code that probes a missing undeclared path
through the C library is NOT detected (the kernel answers ENOENT with no sandbox decision), so these
checks do not prove undeclared absence probes cannot happen; elapsed-time clocks (monotonic, perf
counters, CPU time) and file timestamps are real; random generators in native libraries that read OS
entropy themselves are not intercepted; deliberate tampering with the guard's own hooks, finders or
patched functions is out of scope (removal of the import hook or finder is detected). Scope: job
code is trusted project code. The kernel
filesystem and network sandbox is the enforcement; the Python guard is additional detection of
accidental undeclared dependencies, not an adversarial Python jail, and these checks do not intercept
all nondeterminism or absence probes. This scope MUST NOT excuse an ordinary API bug in a supported
check. Unit code MUST NOT derive outputs from real clocks, file timestamps or native entropy;
clean-room and determinism fixtures remain required. See
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_python_worker.py, test_build_v2_python_sandbox.py,
test_build_v2_python_job_libraries.py and tests/staging.rs.

Private transaction directories MUST actually be empty before cleanup clears the journal;
unknown private leaves MUST preserve the active barrier and evidence. Only checkout output-parent
directories MAY remain populated. See unknown_private_cleanup_leaves_preserve_journal_and_block_readers
in tests/installs.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;safety] build-v2-local-completion-capabilities
Recorded identities MUST validate the exact complete prepared record without probing payload objects;
they MUST NOT certify byte availability or convert into available group/staging tokens. CurrentSources
MUST come from the shared receipt validator under read custody with no-follow pinned file descriptors,
and clone only certified consumer content/mode views with pre/post observations. Custody ends after
staging independent job clones, before running a worker. No copy, hash or live-path reopen is permitted.
FrozenCompletion MUST validate/hash independent snapshots once and retain them across cache publication
failure. Local installation MUST reuse the existing journal/ownership/receipt engine without opening
CAS or claiming a StoredHit; known semantic conflicts MUST refuse before mutation. Local scopes and
real owner/worker evidence remain independent from shared CAS claims and MUST be preserved on failure.
See tests/results.rs metadata lookup cases and tests/installs.rs current/local completion scenarios.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-independent-oracle
The test harness oracle MUST derive expected roots, order, typed edges, run sets and target outputs
from its own fixture specification, without calling production key, graph, store or plan parsing.
The fake adapter MAY use the fixture worker and wire/data types only. See tests/harness.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-target-only-clean-comparison
A build comparison MUST compare only explicitly requested target outputs against a fresh empty-store
rebuild, and MUST reject a stale hit or a missing target output. See tests/harness.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-pending-proof-not-pass
A harness report MUST NOT report a pass while real A5/A9 engine integration or native worker proof
is pending, even when every fake-adapter check succeeds. See tests/harness.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-seeded-reproduction
A seeded graph, edit or store-failure mismatch MUST carry the seed and ordered steps needed to
reconstruct the scenario, and the same seed MUST rebuild the same scenario. See tests/harness.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-selected-source-retention
Selected recorded item sources MUST validate only requested fixed items and persist their digest
claims under the shared GC mutex before exposing a borrowed provider. In-memory claims MUST NOT
advance if persistence fails, including the existing strict full-hit path. Providers MUST use their
transaction's own object store and refuse unclaimed digests, with clone-only restoration and no
payload hashing. Metadata-only retention MUST root the exact sealed record before claim release
without asserting byte availability. Opt-in installed cached sources MUST retain live claims until
explicit finish_sources, even after root success; normal commit semantics remain unchanged.
Committed local plans MUST retain their private completion proof for store-only sibling staging.
See recorded_retention_roots_metadata_without_payload_claims_and_rejects_cross_store,
selected_recorded_sources_require_durable_claims_and_preserve_clone_independence in tests/results.rs,
and retained_restore_sources_survive_settlement_until_explicit_release in tests/installs.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-pure-cleanup-policy
Cleanup fact planning MUST validate all supplied producer/object references before proposing any
removal, protect roots/retained lease sets/recent/unknown observations and producer closure, and
never propose a producer while a remaining consumer references it. Unknown lease lineage and cyclic
closure MUST retain. One absolute deadline covers validation/planning without reset and returns no
plan on expiry. Plans MUST remain diagnostic, with no deletion authority, process-liveness decision,
filesystem access, physical-space claim or new cache identity. See tests/cleanup.rs and
cleanup::tests::deadline_covers_validation_and_planning_without_returning_partial_authority.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-unreal-native-context
An Unreal session's `UnrealContext` MUST bind the BuildId, the editor compile, the declared project
modules, each declared engine plugin, each project plugin (the editor-only `AtelierBuildWorker`
among them) and the declared `-ini:`/`-ForceDPCVars=` settings by content identity (digests of the
produced bytes, never compile keys or locations). Its profile is scheduling only: semantic ini,
CVars and module bytes still enter each unit's key. Before `hello`, once per session, the worker
MUST recompute each declared engine plugin's identity (its descriptor and `Binaries`) from the folder
the editor loaded it from, read every declared setting back from the editor (each forced CVar's
value and each ini key's effective value), write the session evidence file `unreal-context.json`
with what the editor actually loaded and holds, and MUST NOT say `hello` when that differs from the
declared context (an ignored or overridden setting is a difference). A setting the editor does not
hold MUST NOT match, whatever the declared text (a literal `None` included); ini values MUST compare
as exact text, and forced CVars as exact text or as the same finite decimal value, never through a
binary float. Each raw readback MUST be kept in the evidence (`settings_read`). Named gap: engine plugins
enabled by default and engine modules are bound only by the BuildId, not by their bytes. The
controller MUST refuse the session before its first `Run` when that evidence is missing, malformed,
of another version or different. A job's import tables MUST go to `evidence/imports.json`, outside
`output/`, covering exactly the saved packages, each read from the saved file's own import table
(path, class, table order), never from asset-registry dependencies, with each path in Unreal's form
(`.` after the package, `:` only at the first subobject boundary, `.` for deeper nesting); an unreadable table MUST fail the
job, never pass with a guessed list (the real-editor reader is proven only by the pending T2
session). Missing or malformed import evidence MUST be refused. See tests/unreal.rs
(`the_profile_ignores_locations_and_follows_every_identity_field`,
`contexts_refuse_what_a_session_cannot_load_honestly`,
`context_and_import_evidence_are_required_well_formed_and_exact`,
`undeclared_saves_files_dirty_packages_and_op_errors_fail_and_the_next_job_runs`,
`a_different_native_context_or_a_module_rebuild_never_says_hello`).

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] build-v2-unreal-scratch-project
Each Unreal session MUST run on its own scratch project inside the session folder, never on a game
`.uproject` and never sharing a mutable `Content`, `Saved`, `Intermediate`, `Binaries` or user
folder with another session or checkout. Only the declared editor binaries and each declared
plugin's descriptor and `Binaries` MAY be brought in, as APFS clones (never links) whose bytes MUST
match the declared identities, recorded in a hash receipt and made read-only, so an editor that
tries to rebuild a module fails closed instead of writing. The receipt MUST be checked again after
the session (file list, modes, clone and source bytes). The command line MUST be the declared
editor, the scratch project, the session's frozen worker script (`build-v2-unreal-frozen-worker`), fixed flags, a session `-UserDir`, the DDC flags and
graph (`build-v2-unreal-ddc`) and the declared settings only, with `-nocrashreports`. Unreal is NOT
sandboxed. Each of these engine-wide writes, measured in T2, is an explicit proof gap (named, not
prevented, and not covered by any test): (1) `~/Library/Application Support/Epic/UnrealEngine/5.8/
Saved/Config/MacEditor/EditorSettings.ini` (T2: stopped by `-nowrite`, which the command line
passes); (2) the tool preset JSON under `UnrealEngine/Editor` (T2: written even with `-nowrite`);
(3) the build tool's `UnrealBuildTool/Trace.uba` when the editor's startup platform check runs (T2:
skipped with `UE_SKIP_UBT_SDK_SETUP=1`, which the command line does not set); (4) the Zen install
files (`Common/Zen/Install`), Zen data and the `zen service status` utility (T2: none with the v2
graph; `-NoZenAutoLaunch` alone still runs the utility); (5) crash reports (`5.8/Saved/Crashes` and
crashpad caches) for anything `-nocrashreports` does not cover; and (6) the shared filesystem DDC
(`Common/DerivedDataCache`), which a session refused for its cache graph may already have written
during startup. The T2 write scan compares file times under `~/Library`, so it cannot attribute a
write there to one agent when other agents run at the same time.
See
tests/unreal.rs (`a_scratch_project_clones_only_declared_binaries_read_only_and_checks_their_identity`,
`a_tree_identity_names_paths_and_bytes_and_refuses_links`,
`the_command_line_runs_the_worker_script_on_the_scratch_project_with_declared_settings`,
`a_different_native_context_or_a_module_rebuild_never_says_hello`). The editor-only `AtelierBuildWorker` plugin source MUST live at
`platform/build-v2/unreal/AtelierBuildWorker`, outside every folder a game or v1 enumerates
(`platform/engine/Plugins`, game project folders, `AdditionalPluginDirectories`), MUST NOT be enabled
by any game descriptor, and is cloned only into scratch and micro projects; its compiled binaries are
build products, never committed, and their content identity enters `UnrealContext`. See
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_unreal_worker.py
(`test_the_worker_plugin_source_is_outside_every_folder_a_game_or_v1_enumerates`).

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-unreal-frozen-worker
A context MUST freeze the exact bytes of `unreal_worker.py` and the `protocol.py` it loads when it is
declared, each read through one descriptor opened without following a link or blocking on a FIFO
and checked as a regular file on that descriptor. Each session MUST materialize them read-only in
`<session>/worker/`, and the editor MUST run that copy, which loads its protocol only from its own
folder, never from the source tree, so a later edit or retarget of the source never reaches a
session. The bundle's digest (the content identity of the frozen files: no locations and no
installed engine or tool facts) MUST be exposed on the context and MUST be in the session profile,
so a changed worker is a new session. The launch MUST refuse a session whose frozen copy changed,
and before `hello` the worker MUST report the digest of the files it actually loaded, which MUST
match. C3 proves only that session launch is bound to the frozen bundle and that the digest is
exposed. Named future seam (D4/A9, not proven here): the A3 semantic item/op key binder MUST hash
the exact worker and protocol implementation (this digest), the declared project module and plugin
compiled-output views and the semantic settings; it MUST exclude the installed BuildId, the editor
and engine-plugin bytes and the DDC paths, and source compile-input keys are no substitute for
compiled-output identity. See tests/unreal.rs
(`each_session_runs_a_frozen_worker_bundle_whose_digest_is_session_identity`,
`a_worker_bundle_freezes_only_regular_files_and_never_follows_or_blocks`,
`the_profile_ignores_locations_and_follows_every_identity_field`,
`a_different_native_context_or_a_module_rebuild_never_says_hello`).

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] build-v2-unreal-ddc
Every Unreal session MUST cache derived data only in the persistent, v2-owned folder
`<store root>/unreal-ddc/<engine BuildId>`, never in job or session scratch and never emptied per
job. Ordinary import/finish/author sessions MUST pass `-nowrite -NoZenAutoLaunch`.
Only the fixed native cook verifier, issued with private source-cook evidence, MAY omit
`-NoZenAutoLaunch` for the installed SDK's normal Zen package-store service lifetime; its
session compatibility profile MUST have the distinct `-native-store` suffix. This exception
MUST NOT enable Zen DDC, skip namespace/CB checks, or create an unknown namespace.
Every session MUST retain `-nowrite` and the inline graph
`-DDC=(InstalledEnginePak,V2Local=(Type=FileSystem,Path=<that folder>))`, and those flags, the graph
and the folder MUST be in the session profile, so a change to any of them is a new session and never
a reuse of an old one. The DDC is rebuildable acceleration only: no reuse, key or receipt decision
MAY read it, and store GC MAY drop it whole. Before `hello` the worker MUST read the editor's
effective cache graph from the editor (never from the command line), record it in
`unreal-context.json`, and MUST NOT say `hello` (a setup failure, never a silent fallback) when any
node is a Zen, shared, remote or unknown store, a file-system node outside that folder or a pak other
than the installed engine pak, or when no node is inside that folder. There is no read-only parent
cache. The controller MUST check the recorded graph again before the first `Run`. The installed
engine pak MUST stay read-only: the graph does not show whether a pak was opened for writing, so the
session receipt MUST record the pak's size and modification time and `verify` MUST refuse any
change. Named gaps: the engine-pak check compares only size and modification time, so it is not a
content hash, does not prove the pak was read-only and misses a write that restores both; the T2
probe timings came from tiny inputs (64x64 textures, 16x16 meshes) and
are not representative of real assets, which are measured after C3; the plugin's graph reader is
proven against the real editor only by the pending T2 session; sessions of one engine share the
folder, relying on Unreal's multi-process file-system store (assumed, not proven here). See
tests/unreal.rs (`the_ddc_folder_persists_per_engine_and_its_flags_and_graph_are_session_identity`,
`the_ddc_policy_allows_only_the_v2_folder_and_the_engine_pak`,
`the_command_line_runs_the_worker_script_on_the_scratch_project_with_declared_settings`,
`context_and_import_evidence_are_required_well_formed_and_exact`,
`a_scratch_project_clones_only_declared_binaries_read_only_and_checks_their_identity`,
`a_cache_graph_with_zen_or_a_folder_outside_the_v2_ddc_never_says_hello`) and
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_unreal_worker.py
(`test_the_cache_graph_may_hold_only_the_v2_folder_the_engine_pak_and_memory`).

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-unreal-job-isolation
One editor MUST run one job at a time, starting each with an empty `/Game` and empty `output/`.
Input packages MUST be copied read-only to their logical paths and removed afterwards. The packages
saved during a job MUST be exactly its declared output packages (an undeclared save or file is a
`dependency` failure, a missing required package or an unsaved change is a `job` failure, and a
changed input is a `dependency` failure). Every native package output file MUST belong to a package saved during
the job, companion files included; a package file written any other way is a `dependency` failure.
Every collected file MUST hold exactly the bytes its package's last save wrote: the plugin MUST take
each save's file hashes only after an explicit flush of the save's writes
(`UPackage::WaitForAsyncFileWrites`), and MUST hash only the files that save wrote: its target file,
and each `.uexp`, `.ubulk` or `.uptnl` companion whose stat stamp (device, inode, size, modification
time) differs from the stamp taken just before the save. A file the save left alone, such as a plain
write beside it or the other main extension, is never certified as saved. Each hash MUST stay bound
to the package whose save wrote it: across a job's saves, in order, each file keeps its latest
attestation (so a later save that leaves a companion alone keeps the earlier hash), a file saved by
two packages is a `dependency` failure, and a collected file MUST be attested by its own package's
save. A mismatch, an unhashed file or another package's attestation is a `dependency` failure.
Those SHA1 hashes are an integrity check only and MUST NOT become a key ingredient. Every required
output file MUST exist when the job ends (otherwise a `job` failure). Native package files written into
`output/` directly are a `dependency` failure; they MUST be moved out of `/Game` into `output/`.
An `unreal.finish` unit MAY additionally declare opaque `Data` files at exact `data/` paths:
only those named files MAY be written directly, their required inventory MUST be complete and
regular, owned and unaliased, and they MUST NOT count as native package save evidence.
Unknown files or directories MUST refuse. A failed job's `output/` MAY hold partially
moved files, so the controller MUST collect `output/` only from a completed job.
An `unreal.author` unit MAY instead own one required `JsonData` file under `data/`:
the keyed body MUST return the exact named finite JSON value without file-write permission.
The trusted worker serializes only that declared result after ordinary native read, input,
save, dirty-package and ensure checks; the job MUST save no package. Native context verification,
positive reset, guard cleanup and frozen-result publication MUST still apply. See
`test_native_data_result_owns_one_exact_finite_json_output`.
A package saved more than once to the same file counts once; one saved to more than one file is a
`dependency` failure. A failed ensure during the job is a `job` failure. After every job the worker
MUST restore its Python state, empty `/Game` and the asset registry, unload every package the job
touched, collect garbage synchronously through the plugin (`SystemLibrary.collect_garbage` only
schedules a collection a commandlet never reaches), and confirm each package is gone by name
(`find_object`), never by the unload call's own result. Every console variable that existed before the
job MUST keep its value; one registered during the job MUST still be at its default (a named gap: a
new variable's default is not itself checked). When any of that
fails or raises, the worker MUST still send the job's terminal reply and then exit instead of serving another
job. This is detection, not isolation: native engine state outside these checks is a named T2
limitation. See tests/unreal.rs
(`one_editor_serves_jobs_in_order_with_a_clean_game_folder_between_them`,
`undeclared_saves_files_dirty_packages_and_op_errors_fail_and_the_next_job_runs`,
`a_package_left_loaded_a_changed_setting_or_a_raising_reset_retires_the_editor_after_its_reply`) and
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_unreal_worker.py. The real editor's flush-then-hash order is
proven only by the pending T2 session.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-blender-job-isolation
The Blender job loop MUST run inside the installed background Blender started with
`--factory-startup -b --threads 3 --python-exit-code 1 --disable-autoexec` before its `-P` script, so
admission reads its threads, and MUST serve the same protocol as the Python job loop with its own
worker version. Each job MUST run in a fresh Blender from that same binary, in its staged folder,
with the same flags plus `--python-use-system-env`, the declared environment only, every Blender
user folder and `HOME` pointed at a missing path inside the job folder (a job whose staged folder
already holds that path, as a link or as declared code, MUST be refused as `protocol` before Blender
starts), and the scene reset to an empty factory file before the op runs; no state of one job may reach another. Each job MUST run the
Python job bootstrap, so the Python job isolation contract applies inside it with the Blender
application bundle as its installed platform. On macOS the child MUST run under the same deny-default
kill-on-deny sandbox that lets it execute only the Blender binary, read only the bundle, the named
platform files and its job folder, and write only `output/`; every further kernel allowance MUST be a
reviewed, named rule (GPU user clients, metadata of `/tmp` and the developer folder, kernel-only
`/dev/urandom`, socket binds refused without the kill), and nothing in the home folder may be readable.
Native Blender reads of an existing undeclared path and any other network use MUST fail the job as
`dependency`. In Blender jobs `uuid.uuid4` MUST draw from the declared seed and every other entropy
source stays refused; only module objects loaded by Blender's own startup are exempt from the
undeclared-module check. The production entry MUST have no unsandboxed
mode, and the test-only entry MUST announce a distinct worker version. The Python and Blender loop
commands MUST refuse a non-UTF-8 script path rather than alter it, and MUST convert to the guarded
launcher's command with the program, every argument in order, the environment and the working
folder unchanged. Installed Blender and its
bundled add-ons are platform, not key ingredients. The same limitations and scope as the Python job
isolation contract apply, including native probes of missing paths. See
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_blender_worker.py and tests/blender_jobs.rs, including
job_loop_commands_refuse_a_non_utf8_script_path_instead_of_replacing_it and
a_loop_command_converts_to_the_guarded_launcher_command_field_for_field.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-blender-op-boundary
The unused D2 route MUST retain existing MeshIR schema-2 semantics and complete explicit geometry,
material/channel/transform/collision ownership. A selected piece key MUST bind only its selected
payload view, per-piece parameters and actual code/reference inputs, never a planner key, whole
roster or siblings. Producer in-job semantic checks MUST finish before Completed; consumer MUST
fully decode selected bytes and check its emitted artifact before receipt completion. B2 MUST
independently validate its exact certified frozen inventory, schema/roles/bounds and hash bindings,
without claiming another semantic geometry decode or reading live producer files. Unsupported
formats, roles, incomplete/aliased/linked outputs and ownership-widening settings MUST refuse.
See tests/blender_ops.rs and platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_blender_ops.py. Native geometry
fidelity/determinism, dynamic dispatch and production activation remain separate pending acceptance.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] bounded-private-failure-diagnostics
Failure diagnostics MUST retain at most 4096 UTF8 bytes on the original unit attempt, mark
truncation explicitly and preserve the first diagnostic of each attempt through later errors
and retries. This metadata MUST NOT affect policy, custody, keys, cache or publication decisions.
Flattened driver reports MUST preserve attempt association. Only failed post-driver observations
MAY write a private 0600 no-replace diagnostic.json under their original owned guard parent;
Completed MUST NOT write it. Diagnostic IO failure MUST NOT change or mask the original outcome.
Missing diagnostics MUST stay explicitly unknown, never evidence of cleanup. Messages and private
files MUST NOT be published as CI artifacts or added to the strict controller/A7 report wire.
See session_lifecycle::diagnostic_tests, python_executor::production_tests failure diagnostic
cases and test_build_v2_controller_entry.py failed-target locator test. Actual historical M1 call1
cause remains unknown; no functional retry or fullmixed activation is certified by these tests.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;safety] unknown-install-metadata-refusal
Reader and writer admission MUST refuse unknown install-control entries before interpreting
receipts or mutating installed products. Unknown regular files, directories and links MUST
remain untouched; current install journals retain exclusive recovery semantics. No old control
format or completion credit is adopted. See checkout_locks::tests::unknown_install_metadata_refuses_readers_writers_without_mutation.
